# =====================================================================
#  selfext2.la — STAGE 2: THE ADOPTED ARTIFACT BECOMES EXECUTABLE.
#
#  Stage 0 measured the baseline: adopted artifacts were only ever READ.
#  Stage 1 built the criterion that distinguishes a revision from a copy
#  and from a corruption. Neither made the changed thing RUN.
#
#  ── WHAT THIS EMITS, AND WHY TWO PROGRAMS AND NOT ONE ───────────────
#  A module is not a program. To demonstrate a capability at runtime the
#  organ has to emit something with a MAIN, so this writes a RUNNABLE
#  program built from the grown organ plus a MAIN that exercises the new
#  glyph.
#
#  ★ AND IT EMITS THE PARENT PROGRAM TOO, WITH THE IDENTICAL MAIN.
#  That pair is the whole design. One MAIN, two organs:
#      sx2_parent.la = base organ    + MAIN using TRIPLEDEC -> MUST FAIL
#      sx2_child.la  = grown organ   + MAIN using TRIPLEDEC -> MUST PRINT 12
#  A child that prints 12 proves only that SOMETHING printed 12; the
#  parent failing on the SAME MAIN is what isolates the capability as
#  the thing that changed. Without the parent leg, a MAIN that hardcoded
#  the answer would pass, and so would a child that never grew at all.
#
#  ── THE RED PATH IS THE POINT OF THE STAGE ──────────────────────────
#  An UNVERIFIED extension must not reach execution. So the mode is read
#  from a medium (`.sx2mode`, the pattern autopoiesis.la uses for its
#  generation counter) and in "bad" mode the extension carries a test it
#  fails. The organ must then write NO child program at all -- not a
#  broken one, not one that halts politely. Nothing to run is the only
#  refusal that cannot be mistaken for a run that went badly.
#
#  ── SCOPE, STATED PLAINLY ───────────────────────────────────────────
#  This witnesses "a SEPARATE PROCESS runs the adopted extension, and
#  the parent could not have". It does NOT yet witness "the organ itself
#  begets and execve's that process" -- the bundled, VM-side form the
#  ledger ultimately asks for, where copy_self + execve carry the whole
#  vessel. That is a further step (2b) and it costs codegen minutes;
#  its logical content is the same as this, and its additional content
#  is autonomy, which is stage 6's subject. Saying which of the two is
#  witnessed here matters more than having both today.
# =====================================================================

import("specpipe.la")   # GENERATE META_DEBUG DEF TRIPLE PAIR CONS NIL Z IF TRUE FALSE AND
import("selfext1.la")   # C_VERIFIED S_BASE S_EXT S_BAD HASSUB NOT2

glyph SEQ2 = la a. la b. b
glyph J    = la a. la b. concat(a)(b)

# the MAIN both programs carry, character for character
glyph MAINSRC = "\nglyph MAIN = print(int_to_str(TRIPLEDEC(5)))\n"

glyph MODE = read_file(".sx2mode")
glyph WANT_BAD = HASSUB("bad")(MODE)

# the extension under consideration: the honest one, or the one whose
# OWN test fails
glyph SPEC = IF(WANT_BAD)(la _. S_BAD)(la _. S_EXT)

glyph VERIFIED = C_VERIFIED(SPEC)

# the parent program is always emitted: it is the control, and a control
# that is only written when convenient is not a control
glyph EMIT_PARENT = write_file("sx2_parent.la")(J(GENERATE(S_BASE))(MAINSRC))

# the child program is emitted ONLY if the extension verified
glyph EMIT_CHILD = IF(VERIFIED)
    (la _. SEQ2(write_file("sx2_child.la")(J(GENERATE(SPEC))(MAINSRC)))
               ("emitted — the grown organ is now a runnable program"))
    (la _. "REFUSED — the extension failed its own test; NO child program written")

glyph MAIN = SEQ2(EMIT_PARENT)(print(
    J("selfext2 mode=")(J(IF(WANT_BAD)(la _. "bad")(la _. "ok"))
     (J(" verified=")(J(IF(VERIFIED)(la _. "T")(la _. "F"))
      (J(" | ")(EMIT_CHILD)))))))
